    "role": "user",
    "content": "Circuit: Block 3 - Passive Baxandall tone control. Passive Baxandall bass/treble control with 100k audio-taper pots at mid-rotation. About 27 dB mid-band insertion loss when driven from the triode stage's ~43k output impedance; within +1.3/-0.8 dB of the 1 kHz level from 20 Hz to 20 kHz at the centre settings.\n\nStages: tone = Passive tone control\n\nParts:\n- R301: resistor 47k (stage tone)\n- VR301: potentiometer 100k (stage tone)\n- C301: film_cap 10n (stage tone)\n- C302: film_cap 100n (stage tone)\n- R302: resistor 4.7k (stage tone)\n- R303: resistor 33k (stage tone)\n- C303: film_cap 1n (stage tone)\n- VR302: potentiometer 100k (stage tone)\n- C304: film_cap 10n (stage tone)\n\nNetlist of the healthy circuit (SPICE; node names as in the test points):\n* Differential reference circuit - Block 3: passive Baxandall tone control (standalone)\n* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n* Original generic design written for this project, after the passive form of\n* Baxandall's tone control (Wireless World, 1952). Bass: R301-VR301-R302 divider\n* with C301/C302 bridging the pot sections. Treble: C303-VR302-C304 with the\n* wiper to the output; the bass wiper joins the output through R303.\n* Potentiometers are 100k audio (A) taper set to mid-rotation, which on an A\n* taper leaves ~10 % of the track between wiper and the grounded end. Each pot\n* is modelled as upper track (A), lower track (B) and a 1 ohm wiper contact (W).\n* Fixtures: source with 43k output impedance (the triode stage's Ra || rp) and a\n* 100k load (the op-amp stage bias resistor).\n* Run standalone: ngspice -b circuits/tone/tone.cir\n* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n.include ../lib/devices.lib\n\n* ---- Fixtures ----\nVIN_T tone_src 0 DC 0 AC 1 SIN(0 1 1k)\nRSRC_T tone_src tone_in 43k\nRLOAD_OP tone_out 0 100k\n\n* ---- Bass section ----\nR301 tone_in bass_a 47k\nRVR301A bass_a bass_t 90k\nRVR301B bass_t bass_b 10k\nRVR301W bass_t bass_w 1\nC301 bass_a bass_w 10n\nC302 bass_w bass_b 100n\nR302 bass_b 0 4.7k\nR303 bass_w tone_out 33k\n\n* ---- Treble section ----\nC303 tone_in treb_a 1n\nRVR302A treb_a treb_t 90k\nRVR302B treb_t treb_b 10k\nRVR302W treb_t tone_out 1\nC304 treb_b 0 10n\n\n.control\nset noaskquit\nac dec 5 10 100k\nlet gdb = db(mag(v(tone_out)))\nprint gdb\n.endc\n.end\n\nTest points:\n- TP10: node tone_in, Tone-control input (stage tone)\n- TP11: node bass_w, Bass control wiper (stage tone)\n- TP12: node tone_out, Tone-control output (stage tone)\n\nMeasurements (key | what | healthy reading and range | cost):\n- dc:TP10 | DC voltage at TP10 | 0 \u00b5V (range -822 \u00b5V to 822 \u00b5V) | cost 1\n- dc:TP11 | DC voltage at TP11 | 0 \u00b5V (range -822 \u00b5V to 822 \u00b5V) | cost 1\n- dc:TP12 | DC voltage at TP12 | 0 \u00b5V (range -822 \u00b5V to 822 \u00b5V) | cost 1\n- ac:TP10 | 1 kHz signal level (gain from input) at TP10 | 0.539 V/V (-5.4 dB) (range 0.509 V/V (-5.9 dB) to 0.571 V/V (-4.9 dB)) | cost 3\n- ac:TP11 | 1 kHz signal level (gain from input) at TP11 | 0.0485 V/V (-26.3 dB) (range 0.0449 V/V (-27.0 dB) to 0.0525 V/V (-25.6 dB)) | cost 3\n- ac:TP12 | 1 kHz signal level (gain from input) at TP12 | 0.0449 V/V (-27.0 dB) (range 0.0415 V/V (-27.6 dB) to 0.0486 V/V (-26.3 dB)) | cost 3\n- ac20:TP12 | 20 Hz response (gain from input) at TP12 | 0.0509 V/V (-25.9 dB) (range 0.0409 V/V (-27.8 dB) to 0.0633 V/V (-24.0 dB)) | cost 3\n- ac20k:TP12 | 20 kHz response (gain from input) at TP12 | 0.0406 V/V (-27.8 dB) (range 0.0313 V/V (-30.1 dB) to 0.0527 V/V (-25.6 dB)) | cost 3\n- lift:<ref> | desolder one lead of a part and test it out of circuit | result: within or out of tolerance | cost 10 (12 for parts on high-voltage nodes)\n\nFault list (name faults exactly like this):\n- R301:open: R301 open circuit\n- R301:short: R301 short circuit\n- R301:drift_x0.5: R301 value drifted to 0.5x\n- R301:drift_x2: R301 value drifted to 2x\n- R301:drift_x10: R301 value drifted to 10x\n- VR301:wiper_open: VR301 wiper open\n- VR301:track_open: VR301 track open\n- C301:open: C301 open circuit\n- C301:short: C301 short circuit\n- C302:open: C302 open circuit\n- C302:short: C302 short circuit\n- R302:open: R302 open circuit\n- R302:short: R302 short circuit\n- R302:drift_x0.5: R302 value drifted to 0.5x\n- R302:drift_x2: R302 value drifted to 2x\n- R302:drift_x10: R302 value drifted to 10x\n- R303:open: R303 open circuit\n- R303:short: R303 short circuit\n- R303:drift_x0.5: R303 value drifted to 0.5x\n- R303:drift_x2: R303 value drifted to 2x\n- R303:drift_x10: R303 value drifted to 10x\n- C303:open: C303 open circuit\n- C303:short: C303 short circuit\n- VR302:wiper_open: VR302 wiper open\n- VR302:track_open: VR302 track open\n- C304:open: C304 open circuit\n- C304:short: C304 short circuit\n\nBudget: 40 effort units.\n\nCustomer complaint: Evening all, I've been messing about with an old channel strip I rescued from a skip. Something just sounds off but I can't describe it. It's pretty subtle, to be fair. Any ideas would be massively appreciated!\n\nDiagnose the unit. (Session 3 of 3.)"
